# sofarhyd2mqtt

Exposes a Sofar HYD 5…20KTL-3PH hybrid inverter to MQTT following the
[Homie 5 convention](https://homieiot.github.io/). Talks to the inverter over Modbus TCP through an
RS485 gateway.

## Usage

```
sofarhyd2mqtt mqtt --tcp gateway.local:502 --mqtt-broker mqtt://broker:1883?client_id=sofarhyd
sofarhyd2mqtt dump --tcp gateway.local:502
```

`--tcp` is the address of the gateway, which is expected to speak Modbus TCP and relay it to the
RS485 bus. `--unit-id` is the Modbus address of the inverter (1 by default).
`SOFARHYD2MQTT_LOG=debug` makes it more talkative.

`dump` reads the inverter once and prints every property. It never writes.

### Writes

By default **nothing is ever written** to the inverter: no property is settable. Pass
`--allow-writes` to be able to change the settings marked settable below. After a set, the value
the inverter actually has is published, even if it is unchanged, so a controller can tell whether
the inverter took it.

Setting `inverter/sync-clock` to `now` sets the clock of the inverter to the local time of the
system the bridge runs on.

### Polling

`--poll-period` (4 seconds by default) is how often the state of the inverter is read. The energy
counters are read every 15 seconds, the settings every 30 seconds, and the serial number and the
versions every 10 minutes. `--unavailable-after` (60 seconds by default) is for how long the
inverter can go without responding before it is `disconnected`. `--timeout` (3 seconds) and
`--request-gap` (20 ms) tune the requests.

The PV inputs and the batteries are as the inputs of the inverter are set up, up to 4 of each.

## Devices

* **`sofarhyd`** is the bridge: the root device, without nodes. `--device-id` changes it.
* **`sofarhyd-<serial number>`** is the inverter, the child of the bridge. The serial number is
  lowercased, with each run of anything but letters and digits made into a hyphen.

The inverter is published once everything has been read; the bridge can be `ready` without
children until then. While the inverter does not respond, it is `disconnected`. If its inputs are
set up differently, it is published anew.

## Nodes and properties of the inverter

**Positive power is power into the house's system**: buying from the grid and charging the
battery are positive, selling and discharging are negative. The powers of what the inverter puts
(`inverter/output-power`, the phases, the `eps` node) are positive when it puts power out.

| Node | Property | Type | Unit | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `inverter` | `state` | enum | | `waiting`, `checking`, `on-grid`, `off-grid` (on the EPS output), `fault`, `permanent-fault`, `updating`, `self-charging` |
| | `faults` | JSON | | the active faults, alarms and reasons for derating, as `["ID162 RemoteShutdown", …]`, the ID being what the display shows |
| | `enabled` | boolean | | settable. `false` turns the inverter off |
| | `storage-mode` | enum | | settable. `self-use`, `time-of-use`, `timing`, `passive`, `peak-shaving` |
| | `output-power` | integer | W | the AC power that the inverter puts out, to the grid and the EPS output together |
| | `ambient-temperature`, `heatsink-temperature`, `internal-temperature` | integer | °C | |
| | `insulation-resistance` | integer | kΩ | |
| | `clock` | datetime | | settable. The inverter's clock has no time zone. Setting an instant (with an offset) sets the local time of the bridge's system at that instant |
| | `sync-clock` | enum | | settable only, not retained. `now` sets the clock to the bridge's local time. Only there with `--allow-writes` |
| `grid` | `power` | integer | W | at the meter or CT |
| | `reactive-power` | integer | var | at the meter or CT |
| | `frequency` | float | Hz | |
| `load` | `power` | integer | W | what the house uses |
| `eps` | `mode` | enum | | settable. `disabled`, `enabled`, `enabled-with-cold-start` (the EPS output can start from the battery alone) |
| | `power` | integer | W | of the EPS output |
| | `frequency` | float | Hz | |
| `l1`, `l2`, `l3` | `voltage` | float | V | of the phase |
| | `output-current`, `output-power` | | A, W | what the inverter puts out on the phase |
| | `eps-voltage`, `eps-current`, `eps-power` | | V, A, W | of the EPS output on the phase |
| `pv` | `power` | integer | W | of all the PV inputs together |
| | `external-power` | integer | W | of an external (AC coupled) PV inverter |
| `pv-N` | `voltage`, `current`, `power` | | V, A, W | for each PV input, counted from 1 |
| `battery` | `voltage`, `current`, `power` | | V, A, W | |
| | `temperature` | integer | °C | |
| | `state-of-charge`, `state-of-health` | integer | % | |
| | `cycles` | integer | # | |
| `energy` | `solar-today`, `consumed-today`, `imported-today`, `exported-today`, `charged-today`, `discharged-today` | float | kWh | |
| | `solar-total`, `consumed-total`, `imported-total`, `exported-total`, `charged-total`, `discharged-total` | float | kWh | |
| `passive` | `mode` | enum | | settable. `auto`, `manual` or `scheduler`: which settings the passive mode follows. Only those of `manual` are exposed |
| | `grid-power` | integer | W | settable. The desired grid power |
| | `battery-min-power`, `battery-max-power` | integer | W | settable. The bounds of the battery power |
| | `export-limit`, `import-limit` | integer | W | settable. How much may be sold to and bought from the grid |
| | `timeout` | integer | s | settable. `0:65535`, 0 for none. The `timeout-action` is taken if the passive mode settings are not set again within this long |
| | `timeout-action` | enum | | settable. `standby` or `previous-mode` (the storage mode from before the passive mode) |
| `identification` | `serial-number`, `hardware-version` | string | | |
| | `communication-firmware`, `primary-firmware`, `secondary-firmware` | string | | as in `V120005` |
| | `safety-version` | string | | the version of the country (safety) settings, as in `10.08` |

With more than one battery the nodes are `battery-1`, `battery-2` and so on.

A value that is not valid (an unknown state, a state of charge above 100 %, a clock that is not a
date and so on) is not published: the last valid value stays.

The time-of-use, timing and peak shaving schedules and the installer settings (battery
configuration, feed-in limit and so on) are not exposed: use the inverter's menu or app for those.

## Caveats

* The clock can only be set to a year up to 2099.
